                  </origin>
                  <provenance source="2587"><orgName role="fmo" key="org_198">Eton, Buckinghamshire. Royal
                        College of the Assumption of Saint Mary the Virgin</orgName><p>"Liber
                        decretorum romanorum pontificum et incipit in 2o folio &lt;-&gt;tes viii"
                        (cf. MS.22).</p></provenance>
               <provenance type="#m" source="2693"><orgName role="fmo" key="org_1">Exeter, Devon. Cathedral
                        church of St Peter</orgName><p>Notes in the hand of Bishop John Grandison,
                        see esp. fol. 137r: 'Nota hic quod papa se purgauit suspicione volens carere
                        non ex necessitate . . . J Ex'. Identifiable by the opening words of the
                        first leaf of text (fol. ivv) 'In Italia' with the 'Breviarium Canonum
                        Apostolorum in magno volumine quod sic incipit In Ytalia pret' ijlib' in the
                        Exeter Catalogue of 1327 (Oliver, Lives, p. 304).</p><note type="MLGB3_medievalCatalogueNotes">Cat., p. 304</note></provenance>
